course: dictionary
lesson: 2344
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning with a number. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning is used. «Six weeks on crutches.» The words are about walking and getting better, so crutches must be the sticks people use to walk.
explain: «He landed badly, twisted his ankle and spent the next two weeks on crutches.» Twisted and landed badly tell you he was hurt, so the crutches are the sticks that help him move. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the clues around the word?
explain: A crutch can also mean something you lean on too much for support or comfort. If you use something as a crutch, you depend on it. The words around the crutch tell you which meaning the writer chose.
fact: A crutch is a long stick with a support for under the arm or a handle.
fact: Crutches help someone walk when a leg or foot is injured.
fact: Useful phrases are «on crutches», «a pair of crutches» and «use something as a crutch».
fact: A crutch can also mean something you depend on too much for support or comfort.
fact: To find the right meaning, read the words around the word and try each meaning in the sentence.
exercise: «He spent two weeks on crutches.» What are crutches here? | *Sticks to help someone walk when a leg is hurt | Wheels for a bike | Bags for carrying shopping | Shoes for running fast
exercise: Maya says, «I use my notes as a crutch.» What does crutch mean here? | A soft cushion for her back | A kind of bread | *Something she depends on too much for support | A long stick to help her walk
exercise: «After the fall, Sam needed ___ to get to school.» Which word fits the gap? | kettles | *crutches | cushions | trumpets
test: «Six weeks on crutches.» How long is the person on crutches? | Sixteen years | Six days | Six hours | *Six weeks
test: Why might someone use a crutch? | To cut paper | *To help them walk when a leg or foot is injured | To keep the rain off | To carry water to the sink
exam: «He twisted his ankle and was on crutches for weeks.» What was the injury? | A runny nose | A cut finger | A sore throat | *A twisted ankle
